# Twenty Live Schema Snapshot — 2026-09

Observed through authenticated, read-only Twenty REST calls. No write was attempted. This is an integration snapshot, not a permanent field catalogue; refresh it before implementation if workspace metadata changes.

## Connectivity

- `TWENTY_BASE_URL` and `TWENTY_API_KEY` were present.
- `GET /rest/metadata/objects`, `GET /rest/metadata/fields`, `GET /rest/companies` and `GET /rest/people` returned HTTP 200.
- Write scope, custom-field creation, Person creation, association creation and read-back reconciliation remain unverified.

## Objects and relationship

- Company object ID: `89cb0885-61c0-4d39-989f-b7f0cf248dc9`; 39 active fields.
- Person object ID: `4220f12d-d3ec-4268-ad2f-64c4453859fa`; 24 active fields.
- `Company.people`: `ONE_TO_MANY`.
- `Person.company`: `MANY_TO_ONE`, joined by `companyId`; Company deletion sets the relation to null.

Observed records: 40 Companies and 35 People. Thirty-five Companies had one linked Person and five had none; all People were linked. The live schema supports multiple People even though the current A1 population showed at most one.

## Relevant Company fields

Existing business fields include `name`, `domainName`, `address`, `linkedinLink`, `phone`, `email`, `country`, `state`, `city`, `sourceUrl`, `segment`, `discoveryStatus`, `discoverySourceNotes`, `discoveryFingerprint`, `qualificationStatus`, `icpScoreStatus`, `icpScore`, `icpBand`, `icpOutcome`, `evidenceConfidenceScore`, `evidenceConfidenceLevel`, `websitemissing`, `wrongpeople`, and relation `people`.

Meaningful coverage observed:

- name, segment and structured address: 40/40;
- domain URL: 6/40;
- Company phone number: 3/40;
- Company email: 0/40;
- Company LinkedIn URL: 0/40;
- custom city: 20/40; custom state/country: 40/40.

The low domain coverage confirms that domain cannot be a required enrichment gate. Prefer structured address components over the less-complete custom city field for domainless matching inputs when the provider supports them.

## Relevant Person fields

Existing fields include `name`, `emails`, `linkedinLink`, `jobTitle`, `phones`, and relation `company`/`companyId`.

Meaningful coverage observed:

- names and Company links: 35/35;
- phone number: 30/35;
- email: 7/35;
- job title: 0/35;
- LinkedIn URL: 0/35.

Name normalization issue: all 35 People had an empty `lastName`; 34 had whitespace inside `firstName`, indicating that a full name is usually stored in `firstName`. Preserve the source object, derive a normalized lookup name, and create new People with correct first/last components when supported by verified provider data.

